        "problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{2} \\left\\langle 2e^{t},\\, 6t^2\\right\\rangle\\, \\textrm d t.$",
        "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\u27e82{e}^{t},\\,6{t}^{2}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9. \\\\  & =\u27e82{e}^{t}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8[2{e}^{2}-2{e}^{0}],\\,[2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0]\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82{e}^{2}-2,\\,16\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
